# Directories where too much temp stuff may lay around
# SALVAGE-SEPT: was a blanket `tests`, which also swallowed the test sources.
# Ignore the built artefacts but keep tests/src (the .c/.m/.cpp and their
# .stdout goldens). tests/vendor/ stays ignored: fakesdk/ is a symlink farm
# and macosx-sdk-flat.tar.gz is a fat binary blob.
tests/*
!tests/src

# The upstream rule was a bare `tests`, which matches a path component named
# `tests` at ANY depth, not just the top-level one. `tests/*` above is anchored
# to the root, so keep the original breadth for nested directories — otherwise
# subtrees that used to be ignored become untracked noise in `git status`.
src/**/tests/

